NoInlineComponents inlines user components into the app root, and a component
nothing instantiates is unreachable from it -- so it is dropped, and the fyne
output holds nothing of `standalone`. The window is what makes the question
answerable: it is the root, and a component no root reaches is a declaration
the program does not render.

The pass leaves a package with *no* root alone instead, since every component
there is its own entry point and dropping what it cannot reach would empty the
program. That form is a library package, which a golden cannot hold -- a
golden compiles a program, and a program declares a window -- so it is pinned
by `sngl generate sngl:platform/gtk4` in
cmd/sngl/testdata/program_needs_a_window.txt.

The other form, a window as the root of a program that *does* render its
components, is in inline_window_form_anon.txtar.

-- lone.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

component standalone node {
    vbox {
        text(value="standalone")
    }
}

output { go { fyne } }

window {
}
-- out/go/fyne/model.go --
